    "intro_html":  "Fried rice was invented to use up yesterday\u0027s rice, which makes it the original meal prep dish. Restaurants cook it in enormous batches all day long, so scaling this to fourteen containers is not some clever adaptation. It is just how the dish has always been made. Pork tenderloin, egg, peas, carrots, and a hit of sesame oil at the end. Use cold rice from the fridge and you get separate, chewy grains. Use warm rice and you get porridge, so plan ahead by a day.",
